tcs|n|One who entertains for another such sentiments of esteem, respect, and affection that he seeks his society aud welfare; a wellwisher; an intimate associate; sometimes, an attendant. ; One not inimical or hostile; one not a foe or enemy; also, one of the same nation, party, kin, etc., whose friendly feelings may be assumed. The word is some times used as a term of friendly address. ; One who looks propitiously on a cause, an institution, a project, and the like; a favorer; a promoter; as, a friend to commerce, to poetry, to an institution. ; One of a religious sect characterized by disuse of outward rites and an ordained ministry, by simplicity of dress and speech, and esp. by opposition to war and a desire to live at peace with all men. They are popularly called Quakers. ; A paramour of either sex.	a:1bih,77,3;i27,71,5;16yt,69,2;nc7,69,5;w8h,69,7;iy9,68,1;1bl9,53,6;zoi,52,4;1ihy,52,1;14xm,48,2;13gx,45,5;18de,42,5;243v,40,2;18k7,38,4;269i,37,3~7c0,5,19;d9o,5,11;1hx0,5,7;w8h,69,7;1vib,14,7;c9m,28,6;1bl9,53,6;17n4,30,5;13gx,45,5;18de,42,5;nc7,69,5;sxp,25,5;i27,71,5;qxu,9,5;qzb,29,5	v:zwr,66,5;w8h,41,1;243m,37,10;c7p,36,1;8uz,23,1;1o5b,22,2;269i,21,1;hwt,15,1;28dj,5,2~243m,37,10;zwr,66,5;28dj,5,2;1o5b,22,2;w8h,41,1;c7p,36,1;269i,21,1;8uz,23,1;hwt,15,1	V:16ki,93,3;ur5,64,3;1pmb,49,5;8o5,48,2;1bk,45,5;27y6,42,2;s76,39,4;132b,39,3;8o4,38,2;20mf,35,4;1pmd,34,3;2371,33,4;16j7,32,4;1fjv,32,4;1qux,32,1~1z7i,23,14;1rn5,4,9;22lf,26,8;2809,18,7;221d,7,7;1bss,7,7;1o0f,13,6;1ofl,13,6;22p8,11,6;16sq,12,6;1gpw,23,6;abe,1,6;29dl,21,6;gj2,1,6;uup,3,6	n:5el,72,6;iy9,68,1;1ihy,62,2;c7p,61,6;14xm,54,3;5d5,53,4;15hh,46,4;hfm,40,5;uty,37,4;4rt,33,3;18x,32,4;269i,31,2;qdx,25,5;zfz,24,3;8uz,23,1~1siy,8,8;1yhg,1,7;5el,72,6;qz3,11,6;1luo,7,6;c7p,61,6;1ixs,7,6;qdx,25,5;hfm,40,5;18x,32,4;15hh,46,4;5d5,53,4;uty,37,4;14xm,54,3;4rt,33,3	N:15rm,84,5;b26,65,3;vcj,55,2;1qux,52,4;28dp,50,2;8o4,44,3;jz0,30,7;13uw,26,4;8cw,25,3;ykq,24,3;16j7,22,2;132a,21,1;p3n,20,4;crp,20,4;uv6,18,1~1qlb,17,8;jz0,30